Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Subtitles: translate whichever subtitle is chosen into the
 language chosen

A translation was one more entry in the subtitle list, offered only for
a video with no subtitle in the language the viewer reads, and only into
that language. Now the tracks are translated themselves: the subtitle
dialog has a "Translate to" button, VideoPlayer.SubtitleTranslate shows
what it is on - Off, or a language - and
PlayerControl(SubtitleTranslate) turns it to the next: off, then the
subtitle language chosen in Kodi's settings and the languages subtitles
are downloaded in, in turn. No setting of its own: on a box set to
English with French among the download languages it goes Off, English,
French. Whichever track the viewer chooses is read in that language when
it is text in another, and its name in the list says so ("English
(translated from French)"); a track already in that language is shown as
it is, and its own language is never offered: with it open the button
reads Off. Turning it reopens the subtitle open, translated or not.

A video starts as before: with no subtitle in the language the viewer
reads, translated into it from the track Kodi would choose - the
viewer's own choice of subtitle for the video stands - and untranslated
otherwise. The choice is kept for the film - by its file as the library
knows it, whichever path plays it - in
special://profile/subtitletranslation.json, off included, and it starts
that way when it plays again. The label is empty, and the skin hides the
button, while "AI translate subtitles" is off or no AI provider is
chosen.

The player's hooks stay as they were: the entry of its own is never
offered, so the list is the video's own tracks.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
